WEBVTT

00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:13.840
Bruce...

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:19.080
It is not your daughter, but I, who
shall receive your inheritance.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.700
Well? How does that make you feel?

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:29.420
It's your fault for dying!

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.460
Millennium Doug MK ll...

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:44.510
An interstellar transport shuttle manufactured
by the Millennium Corporation.

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:47.310
Let's see, the model year was...

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:50.640
What?! G.C. 1992?!

00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:56.150
This ship was built the same year
my grandfather was born.

00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:59.420
Will it even move the way it is now?

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:01.120
This says it's still in service, performing admirably.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:04.030
They might as well have foisted
a scrap yard ship on us.

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:06.490
Exchange it for a recent model.

00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:08.700
No way! That'd be a waste.

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:09.860
A waste?

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:12.900
This whole vintage feel is the coolest.

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:14.400
Whoa, awesome!

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:17.510
It says you adjust the descent speed manually!

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.940
Wow, check it out! I wonder what this switch does?

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:22.170
You're the one who's not working properly.

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:24.610
Chelsea? Chelsea!

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:25.940
Come here a minute.

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:28.320
What is it, Angelica?

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:31.010
Would you mind helping me get
these onto the shuttle?

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:35.660
Is this all food?!

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:36.620
Yep.

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:49.300
Franca sure made a fuss, didn't she?

00:01:49.870 --> 00:01:53.370
She didn't have to worry about us
on top of everything else.

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:56.640
You think maybe since she's lived
her whole life around grown-ups

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:59.050
she's learned to be uptight all the time.

00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:00.950
That's exactly why...

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:05.180
once we finish this job I'm gonna let
Franca go back to being a kid.

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:21.030
Time left until the photonic bomb is dropped on Graceland...

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:24.330
72 hours

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:43.120
I etch out today with my finger

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:46.530
on the dusty hood of a car

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:50.000
As the rain shower passed over

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.830
it vanished just like love

00:02:52.940 --> 00:03:00.070
There's something in your heart you can't get rid of

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:06.160
So beat your invisible wings

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:10.540
We'll fight back against the wind

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:13.450
that gusts at us so relentlessly

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:16.860
We'll stand firm against it

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:20.700
with steadfast emotion! Go!

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:27.600
We continue running on our way

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:33.610
to a place promised, where sandstorms whirl

00:03:33.610 --> 00:03:36.740
Tonight is the night

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:40.250
We're gonna make it through

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:47.950
On to our destination

00:03:56.170 --> 00:04:02.130
Episode 8   The Road to Gigabanks

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:58.700
Main engine optimal.

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:01.240
Setting of descent point coordinate axes complete.

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:03.600
All sections green.

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:08.440
All systems operating within normal parameters.

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:11.310
Commence descent to Graceland.

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:24.880
Messenger craft docking at Gate 7.
Cleared for approach.

00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:29.790
I have brought written orders for
Commander-in-Chief Malcolm from Admiral Mill.

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:32.190
Well done.

00:04:32.430 --> 00:04:34.200
By carrier pigeon?

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:35.290
Yes, sir.

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:38.570
The development of communications
and jamming signals

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:41.010
has led to them delivering these by hand
the old-fashioned way, huh?

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:43.410
It has been done in accordance
with the Federation manual,

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:45.280
regarding retention of classified information
and information leakage.

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:48.610
It demonstrates just how vital this mission is, sir.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:50.880
Yes, I guess you're right.

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:54.860
<i>Commander-in-Chief Malcolm, I have good news.</i>

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:57.460
<i>General Boniek of the Graceland Liberation Forces</i>

00:04:57.460 --> 00:05:00.930
<i>has agreed to peace negotiations now,
at the very last moment.</i>

00:05:00.930 --> 00:05:03.900
<i>Preparations for the negotiations are
underway in the utmost secrecy.</i>

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:07.200
Good, it looks like we'll get by
without dropping the bomb.

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:08.860
Yeah...

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:12.840
<i>However, I want you all to continue
on course towards Graceland.</i>

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:16.740
<i>If the Liberation Forces find out that peace
talks are going on behind the scenes,</i>

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:20.340
<i>it's possible that some will not be willing
to look at the big picture.</i>

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:23.990
I suppose this means every organization has
certain reactive members prone to backlash.

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:27.060
<i>Also, the plan is for the peace talks with Boniek
and the leaders of the Liberation Forces</i>

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:28.960
<i>to be carried out aboard your ship.</i>

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:31.530
<i>The Secretary of Foreign Affairs, Senator Hewlett,</i>

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:34.790
<i>who will serve as full ambassador in the
peace talks, is already on his way there.</i>

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:36.730
What is it?

00:05:36.730 --> 00:05:39.800
<i>We have just received word from the
fleet surrounding Graceland</i>

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:43.400
<i>that a single Guild battleship
is descending to Graceland.</i>

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:45.600
A Guild battleship?

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:47.100
All right.

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:48.840
How shall we proceed?

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:51.450
Why now?

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:53.180
To hawk weapons?

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:56.180
It's also possible the Liberation Forces
have called them in.

00:05:56.180 --> 00:06:00.490
Then could agreeing to peace talks
also be a ruse to buy time?

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:03.190
In either event, until they have come
to the negotiating table,

00:06:03.190 --> 00:06:04.990
we cannot afford to aggravate matters in any way.

00:06:04.990 --> 00:06:07.700
Tell the blockade to let them go untouched.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:08.890
Yes, sir.

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:13.670
So you are going to Graceland after all, are you?

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:14.700
Yes.

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:18.110
Thank you very much for the shuttle.
It's totally cool!

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:20.130
I'm at a loss for words.

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:24.150
Actually, I thought this might be enough
to make you give up.

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:25.910
We appreciate it.

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:32.850
A short while ago, a Guild battleship
descended to Graceland.

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:34.660
Did it come into conflict with
the Federation's forces?

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:37.130
No, the Federation has not made
any move against it.

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:40.320
You could say it's more like they let
it slip by without a word.

00:06:40.730 --> 00:06:41.730
Which means...

00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:45.890
The dropping of the photonic bomb
will be carried out as planned.

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:49.100
Whatever the Guild might do will not
affect the state of the war.

00:06:49.100 --> 00:06:51.610
I think that's a reasonable conclusion.

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:53.980
Even so, do you still intend to go?

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:57.070
Yes, it is my job after all.

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:00.150
Descent speed optimal.

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:02.420
Sixty seconds to arrival at destination point.

00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:03.920
Visibility normal.

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:05.690
Touchdown point clear.

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:07.350
Firing reverse thrusters.

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:10.320
Touchdown at destination point.

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:11.990
All personnel prepare to disembark.

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:14.660
All right, then...

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:17.720
We will begin our treasure hunt.

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:20.220
Ah, man...

00:07:20.570 --> 00:07:24.240
Marciano and her gang have probably
started their treasure hunting.

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:26.210
Hey, you're not supposed to mention them.

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:29.080
It makes me feel like there's
no point flying this thing.

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:31.140
Damn it! This is so damn frustrating!

00:07:31.980 --> 00:07:34.910
They'll never be able to find Bruce's inheritance!

00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:38.720
Aren't you forgetting something, Pops?

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:41.360
Those guys have Bruce's eye!

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:43.850
So what if they do?

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:46.260
They're not gonna find it.

00:07:46.260 --> 00:07:50.100
Well, how about that! You're just bubbling
over with confidence, aren't you?

00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:54.070
You said it yourself back when you
watched the video in Bruce's eye,

00:07:54.070 --> 00:07:56.940
that you couldn't believe it was
the same planet at all.

00:07:57.170 --> 00:07:59.010
Is it really that different now?

00:07:59.010 --> 00:08:01.840
It's not that it's simply "different."

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:05.750
Compared to what's in those videos,
Graceland is now...

00:08:06.110 --> 00:08:09.210
It's a whole other planet.

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:15.090
We couldn't possibly determine where
the cave with Gigabanks is now.

00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:23.500
I'm amazed you can eat with
the ship shaking like this!

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:26.430
Don't you feel sick or anything?

00:08:26.430 --> 00:08:29.500
Nah, I'm used to eating inside ships.

00:08:29.500 --> 00:08:34.010
If you've got that much composure,
then I guess you'll be all right,

00:08:34.010 --> 00:08:35.640
no matter what happens.

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:38.410
Well, you see...

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:41.120
We've gone a little off course
from our touchdown point.

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:43.050
Off course?! How far?

00:08:43.050 --> 00:08:47.150
Well, actually, I don't really know myself.

00:08:48.120 --> 00:08:49.990
Hang on!

00:08:49.990 --> 00:08:52.260
You don't know'? What are you talking about?!

00:08:53.330 --> 00:08:57.760
Well, this is the first time I've
ever tried landing manually.

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:12.280
June's squad is commencing search of sector B-6.

00:09:12.450 --> 00:09:15.310
January's squad is moving to sector D-4.

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:19.180
April's squad has completed search of sector A-2.

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:21.480
No sign of Gigabanks.

00:09:21.690 --> 00:09:24.930
August's squad has completed search of sector E-1.

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:26.830
No sign of Gigabanks.

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:30.460
March's squad has completed search of sector C-4.

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:32.590
No sign of Gigabanks.

00:09:32.770 --> 00:09:33.670
Next...

00:09:35.270 --> 00:09:37.400
Guys, listen to me a minute.

00:09:38.570 --> 00:09:40.880
To buy ourselves time to search for the treasure,

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:44.580
we'll have to do something about
the photonic bomb on our own.

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:46.680
We know that, Mister.

00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:51.690
You want to split us into a Jupiter group
and a Gigabanks group, right?

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:53.420
That's right.

00:09:53.420 --> 00:09:56.860
We could also head to Graceland after
we stop the photonic bomb,

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:59.830
but if Marciano beats us to
the treasure, it's all over.

00:09:59.830 --> 00:10:01.700
I'm telling you I know that.

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:05.030
We can't expose Franca to the dangers
involved in getting rid of the bomb.

00:10:05.030 --> 00:10:07.340
We need Katana to pilot the Coyote.

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:10.610
And the old guy here knows all about Gigabanks.

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:12.400
And that leaves me.

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:15.010
It'll be all right. Just leave it to me.

00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:17.770
I just need to stop that photonic bomb, right?

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:23.210
Well, I would like to have you go to Jupiter too.

00:10:24.090 --> 00:10:25.490
Too?

00:10:25.490 --> 00:10:28.460
I also want Swamp to go with you.

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:31.160
Wait a minute, Mister!

00:10:31.160 --> 00:10:33.030
I don't need the old guy.

00:10:33.030 --> 00:10:34.830
He'll only slow me down.

00:10:34.830 --> 00:10:36.590
My sentiments exactly.

00:10:37.830 --> 00:10:40.500
I'll be just fine on my own. Leave this to me.

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:42.440
That's probably what he's worried about.

00:10:42.440 --> 00:10:45.630
Enough of your heckling from the sidelines,
you shrub-headed freak!

00:10:45.810 --> 00:10:48.620
Don't you think this is a bad combination after all?

00:10:46.110 --> 00:10:47.740
You ever consider trying out a new hairdo?

00:10:47.740 --> 00:10:49.120
You don't look any different now

00:10:48.880 --> 00:10:50.170
You think?

00:10:49.110 --> 00:10:50.510
than you did in those old videos!

00:10:50.510 --> 00:10:55.080
You're the one who needs to act your own age,
and at least button your damn shin right.

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:54.580
Looks to me like they're enjoying this.

00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:57.150
I'll bet your mommy used to scold you for
being so sloppy, didn't she?

00:10:57.150 --> 00:10:58.420
Ah, I can't stand it!

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:00.120
Everything you say pisses me off!

00:11:00.120 --> 00:11:03.220
I feel exactly the same way about you.

00:11:03.220 --> 00:11:05.350
I'm gonna get me some scissors and
trim that damn bush on your head.

00:11:04.470 --> 00:11:07.310
Time left until the photonic bomb is dropped on Graceland...

00:11:05.350 --> 00:11:07.520
And I'm gonna button up that damn shin
for you nice and tight!

00:11:07.390 --> 00:11:10.640
59 hours

00:11:21.510 --> 00:11:24.000
I figured out where we are, Angelica!

00:11:24.650 --> 00:11:25.510
Well?

00:11:25.750 --> 00:11:29.920
45 degrees North latitude,
160 degrees East longitude...

00:11:29.920 --> 00:11:32.790
I guess we're at this point here,
on the Paralla Ocean.

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:34.690
Which means...

00:11:34.690 --> 00:11:39.130
We've ended up pretty far from where
Marciano's gang landed.

00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:40.930
Sorry about that...

00:11:40.930 --> 00:11:42.200
It's all right.

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:44.430
It's fine as long as we make it there
before Mister arrives.

00:11:45.070 --> 00:11:48.000
Will Mister really come?

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:49.840
Oh, he'll come.

00:11:49.840 --> 00:11:55.170
In that case, this Mister must be quite the optimist.

00:11:55.810 --> 00:11:57.110
That's right.

00:11:57.110 --> 00:12:00.080
As long as the odds are greater than zero,
he won't give up.

00:12:00.080 --> 00:12:01.580
He wouldn't do us the favor.

00:12:01.580 --> 00:12:04.020
He'll tenaciously cling to his own ideas.

00:12:04.020 --> 00:12:05.990
That's what Coyotes are all about.

00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:07.610
Now you've got it.

00:12:09.590 --> 00:12:11.960
I can't tell if that's a compliment or an insult...

00:12:12.260 --> 00:12:13.760
Well, shall we get going?

00:12:13.760 --> 00:12:14.960
Sure!

00:12:15.100 --> 00:12:18.270
Um, Angelica? Are those...

00:12:18.270 --> 00:12:21.300
The evacuations have begun for real, haven't they?

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:22.770
Yeah...

00:12:22.940 --> 00:12:26.570
Everyone is going to abandon this planet.

00:12:40.020 --> 00:12:41.090
Well?

00:12:41.090 --> 00:12:43.220
Do you think you'll be able to lock
on Jupiter's coordinates?

00:12:43.220 --> 00:12:45.260
Do you have any idea who you're
speaking to, young lady?

00:12:45.260 --> 00:12:46.890
That's right!

00:12:46.890 --> 00:12:49.330
It's no use, no matter what kind of
jamming signals they send out.

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:51.530
They're no match for us!

00:12:55.240 --> 00:12:58.470
March's squad has arrived in sector C-2.

00:12:58.970 --> 00:13:02.180
June's squad has completed
search of sector B-3.

00:13:02.180 --> 00:13:04.410
No sign of Gigabanks.

00:13:04.410 --> 00:13:07.950
January's squad has completed
search of sector D-5.

00:13:07.950 --> 00:13:10.150
No sign of Gigabanks.

00:13:10.150 --> 00:13:13.550
April's squad has completed
search of sector A-4.

00:13:13.550 --> 00:13:15.560
No sign of Gigabanks.

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:20.590
In all seriousness, it seems as though we may have
to cover every square inch of the planet.

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:24.960
Didn't you have something you
wanted to talk about?

00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:29.230
Well, not that it matters to me.

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:32.970
I'll bet you actually enjoy getting on his case.

00:13:32.970 --> 00:13:34.480
I'm on to you.

00:13:34.480 --> 00:13:36.680
Are you talking about Bishop?

00:13:36.680 --> 00:13:39.670
It's probably amusing for you
since he's such a dope!

00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:43.720
Hey, don't go getting a kick
out of this all by yourself.

00:13:43.720 --> 00:13:45.850
Aren't you getting a kick out of it?

00:13:45.850 --> 00:13:48.150
I didn't come here for amusement.

00:13:48.690 --> 00:13:51.090
Well, I'm amused.

00:13:51.360 --> 00:13:56.060
This whole Gigabanks deal is a total blast,
like I thought.

00:13:56.330 --> 00:14:04.570
I don't like how you just keep pressing on without
any doubt that I'll do whatever you say.

00:14:04.710 --> 00:14:06.540
You are though.

00:14:08.710 --> 00:14:11.580
We're gonna stop this
photonic bomb from dropping.

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:13.250
It won't be easy.

00:14:13.250 --> 00:14:15.010
That's the impression I get.

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:17.590
I can't let him go alone.

00:14:17.590 --> 00:14:19.180
I know.

00:14:19.520 --> 00:14:24.760
The thing we've got to consider is what
we're going to Graceland for.

00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:31.190
I've come this far to see for myself whether or not
you're worthy to inherit Bruce's legacy.

00:14:31.630 --> 00:14:33.100
That's the idea.

00:14:34.870 --> 00:14:36.700
Can I ask you something?

00:14:36.700 --> 00:14:38.470
Feel free.

00:14:38.470 --> 00:14:44.240
What did Bruce call to tell you before
he pulled the heist on Gigabanks?

00:14:44.780 --> 00:14:46.940
Nothing at all.

00:14:47.380 --> 00:14:49.580
Can I ask you something?

00:14:49.580 --> 00:14:50.950
What?

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:56.690
Did he... Did Bruce get a kick
out of cracking Gigabanks?

00:15:03.300 --> 00:15:04.600
Shall I help you?

00:15:04.600 --> 00:15:07.030
No, it's all right.

00:15:07.030 --> 00:15:09.240
I'm pretty much done now.

00:15:09.240 --> 00:15:10.900
Ah, okay.

00:15:13.570 --> 00:15:15.210
Say. Franca.

00:15:15.210 --> 00:15:16.570
Hm?

00:15:16.780 --> 00:15:19.840
So do you want Bruce's legacy?

00:15:21.820 --> 00:15:23.310
I'm not sure.

00:15:23.450 --> 00:15:26.390
What would you do if you got hold of
10 billion space dollars?

00:15:26.390 --> 00:15:28.120
What do you mean what would I do?

00:15:28.120 --> 00:15:32.150
With that much money,
you could buy anything you wanted.

00:15:33.190 --> 00:15:37.560
To be honest, I don't really care about money.

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:39.690
Only...

00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:43.400
I would like to know more about Papa.

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:49.080
Everyone calls him the Pirate King, and says
that he was such an amazing person,

00:15:49.080 --> 00:15:51.610
but that's only stuff I've heard.

00:15:51.610 --> 00:15:54.810
We didn't have much time together.

00:15:55.920 --> 00:15:58.220
But I was thinking if I got the treasure,

00:15:58.220 --> 00:16:01.550
I might find out what kind of person he was.

00:16:05.560 --> 00:16:08.230
Time left until the photonic bomb is dropped on Graceland...

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:11.030
48 hours

00:16:16.800 --> 00:16:18.770
That's another Guild helicopter.

00:16:20.170 --> 00:16:25.280
Seeing them flying around all over the place makes
me think they haven't found the treasure yet.

00:16:25.280 --> 00:16:28.320
What could the treasure be anyway?

00:16:28.320 --> 00:16:29.520
Who knows...

00:16:29.520 --> 00:16:32.090
Aren't you interested in finding out what it is?

00:16:32.090 --> 00:16:33.780
Oh, I am.

00:16:33.890 --> 00:16:36.620
Why do you want to know everything?

00:16:36.620 --> 00:16:38.610
I don't get it.

00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:43.330
I can't imagine Mister would come here
with money as his only motive.

00:16:43.330 --> 00:16:45.430
There must be something else.

00:16:45.430 --> 00:16:47.330
I want to know what that is.

00:16:47.630 --> 00:16:51.040
Are you really curious about it
just because it's your job?

00:16:51.670 --> 00:16:54.380
I've been meaning to ask you this for a while...

00:16:54.380 --> 00:16:58.810
ls there something that happened that
motivated you to pursue Mister?

00:16:59.250 --> 00:17:03.440
It was four years ago that you became an
investigator focusing on Mister, right?

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:20.670
How about that!

00:17:20.670 --> 00:17:22.670
The price on my head has gone up again!

00:17:22.670 --> 00:17:25.770
That's hardly anything to be so laid-back about.

00:17:25.770 --> 00:17:29.230
That's gonna have bounty hunters
drooling all throughout space.

00:17:30.010 --> 00:17:31.950
Will this ship do?

00:17:31.950 --> 00:17:34.180
All right, I'll take it.

00:17:34.180 --> 00:17:35.480
I appreciate the business.

00:17:37.380 --> 00:17:39.290
This is too much!

00:17:39.290 --> 00:17:42.620
Not at all. I think it's a fair amount.

00:17:42.620 --> 00:17:45.990
Considering the information you give me, that is.

00:17:47.560 --> 00:17:48.960
Jeez...

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:50.930
C'mon, this is nothing new.

00:17:51.630 --> 00:17:58.670
I don't know the reason why, but some Guild people
are digging up the ground all over Graceland.

00:17:58.670 --> 00:18:00.240
Huh?

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:02.880
One other thing, and this is a rumor,
but supposedly...

00:18:02.880 --> 00:18:07.250
A group of Federation higher-ups
are headed towards Graceland.

00:18:07.610 --> 00:18:09.850
Who's in charge?

00:18:09.850 --> 00:18:12.650
Senator Hewlett...

00:18:15.560 --> 00:18:18.060
What? I can take it, can't I?

00:18:18.060 --> 00:18:19.390
Yeah...

00:18:19.390 --> 00:18:21.790
For a little extra information.

00:18:24.770 --> 00:18:26.870
Well? Any results from the transmission?

00:18:26.870 --> 00:18:29.770
Nope, hang on another minute.

00:18:29.770 --> 00:18:31.140
Whatcha doing?

00:18:31.140 --> 00:18:35.580
We're sending out a signal in all directions
which forces a reply,

00:18:35.580 --> 00:18:37.880
and then testing the response that we get back.

00:18:37.880 --> 00:18:40.080
It's like Mister said.

00:18:40.080 --> 00:18:43.020
There's a single direction we isolated
that isn't returning a reply.

00:18:43.020 --> 00:18:47.820
You can bet there's strong jamming
over that whole area.

00:18:48.220 --> 00:18:50.790
Another thing I heard, which is also a rumor,

00:18:50.790 --> 00:18:53.560
is that there are carrier pigeons
flying all around there.

00:18:54.030 --> 00:18:55.460
Carrier pigeons?

00:18:55.900 --> 00:18:57.560
Regarding the most highly classified orders,

00:18:57.560 --> 00:19:01.670
the Federation manual dictates
the use of jamming signals,

00:19:01.670 --> 00:19:03.500
which also shut out their own side's transmissions.

00:19:03.500 --> 00:19:08.100
All orders are delivered by hand.

00:19:09.310 --> 00:19:14.450
Then that story about the Federation
higher-ups heading for Graceland...

00:19:14.450 --> 00:19:16.420
ls something we can actually believe.

00:19:16.950 --> 00:19:17.920
Guess so.

00:19:17.920 --> 00:19:20.790
So my thinking goes.

00:19:20.950 --> 00:19:26.190
So even if Katana and I try to break into the
Federation's network and find their location,

00:19:26.190 --> 00:19:29.100
we won't get anywhere since
no signals are being broadcast.

00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:30.000
Wow...

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:32.900
You guys are surprisingly on the ball with this.

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:35.100
Franca...

00:19:37.140 --> 00:19:41.600
Well, the time has finally come
for us to really do this thing.

00:19:42.040 --> 00:19:43.170
Here.

00:19:44.380 --> 00:19:46.010
What's that for?

00:19:46.010 --> 00:19:48.780
I figured you wouldn't have one.

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:50.420
It's the latest model though,

00:19:50.420 --> 00:19:53.720
so it might be a little tough
for an old geezer to use.

00:19:53.720 --> 00:19:55.790
Well, I guess you are the kind of guy

00:19:55.790 --> 00:19:58.720
who compensates for his lack of skill
with fancy equipment.

00:20:03.800 --> 00:20:07.060
Wow, you're good, Swamp!

00:20:09.570 --> 00:20:12.410
I'm going to do as you say this time.

00:20:12.410 --> 00:20:13.970
Yeah, yeah.

00:20:13.970 --> 00:20:17.410
I'm sure I'll have to sit through one of
your sermons when we get back.

00:20:18.710 --> 00:20:20.080
Naturally.

00:20:20.080 --> 00:20:24.110
If you guys screw this up, we're dead meat.
We're counting on ya.

00:20:24.520 --> 00:20:25.650
We're counting on ya!

00:20:25.650 --> 00:20:27.750
You just leave it to us.

00:20:27.750 --> 00:20:30.520
Well, if we're all decided, then let's get ready to go!

00:20:30.860 --> 00:20:33.160
We don't have much time!

00:20:56.250 --> 00:20:59.380
You called, Mother?

00:21:01.090 --> 00:21:03.220
I have an errand for you.

00:21:12.500 --> 00:21:13.500
\h\h\h\h\h\hRECEIPT 

00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:13.750
I took 20 gallons of gas.

00:21:26.310 --> 00:21:29.280
The Twelve Sisters' fighters?

00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:34.020
<i>Hoho o tsutawaru
Where are these waterdrops</i>

00:21:34.020 --> 00:21:44.330
<i>shizuku doko Kara kuru no
that travel along my cheek coming from?</i>

00:21:44.330 --> 00:21:48.460
<i>Oshiete...
Tell me...</i>

00:21:50.870 --> 00:22:02.150
<i>Makimodosenai jikan to iu ruuru ni</i>

00:21:50.870 --> 00:22:02.150
<i>I grabbed the rule that says we can't turn back time</i>

00:22:02.150 --> 00:22:08.800
<i>munagura tsukanda
by the collar</i>

00:22:06.990 --> 00:22:08.490
Hey, Mister.

00:22:08.490 --> 00:22:09.970
Yeah? What's up?

00:22:09.560 --> 00:22:13.270
<i>Koko ni aru "omoi" de sae 
I resist the fading memories</i>

00:22:10.460 --> 00:22:14.980
I think that dealing with the bomb on his own 
would definitely be a lot of trouble for Bishop,

00:22:13.290 --> 00:22:23.440
<i>usuragu kioku ni teikou suru keredo 
even with the feelings here</i>

00:22:14.960 --> 00:22:18.830
but will you really be all right 
at Gigabanks without Swamp?

00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:21.340
Swamp said so himself,

00:22:21.340 --> 00:22:26.070
that the Graceland in the video was 
a whole other planet from what it is now.

00:22:23.940 --> 00:22:27.030
<i>Kitto koroshi ni kuru 
But I'm sure they'll come to kill me</i>

00:22:27.570 --> 00:22:33.740
<i>Sugite kita hibi no naka de
From out of all the days that have gone by</i>

00:22:28.040 --> 00:22:30.780
We'll probably figure something out.

00:22:31.140 --> 00:22:33.010
Probably?

00:22:34.050 --> 00:22:42.520
<i>tatta hitotsu shinjirareru
there's only one thing I can believe in</i>

00:22:42.520 --> 00:22:48.860
<i>Koe o karasete naita
I cried until my voice was hoarse</i>

00:22:48.860 --> 00:22:52.200
<i>Koko e kite
Come to me</i>

00:22:52.200 --> 00:22:55.180
<i>Soba ni ite
Be by my side</i>

00:22:53.670 --> 00:22:55.170
Ready to go.

00:22:55.170 --> 00:22:55.870
No problems here either.

00:22:55.810 --> 00:22:57.800
<i>Nee
Okay?</i>

00:22:55.870 --> 00:22:57.170
No problems here either.

00:22:57.730 --> 00:23:00.370
So we're doing this together, huh?

00:23:00.840 --> 00:23:03.210
Want me to give you a sermon?

00:23:04.810 --> 00:23:07.610
Mister, this is from Swamp.

00:23:09.080 --> 00:23:10.680
It's a compass, right?

00:23:10.680 --> 00:23:11.820
Yeah...

00:23:11.820 --> 00:23:15.380
He could have just given it to you
himself instead of asking me.

00:23:16.520 --> 00:23:19.330
What? A present from Swamp?

00:23:19.330 --> 00:23:20.760
Yeah!

00:23:20.760 --> 00:23:23.790
It's a map. To Gigabanks!

00:23:25.230 --> 00:23:26.470
They're off.

00:23:26.470 --> 00:23:32.340
<i>Oyasumi no kisu no ato mo
I won't forget that we were also together</i>

00:23:31.610 --> 00:23:33.550
Our lives are on the line here!

00:23:32.740 --> 00:23:41.100
<i> lssho datta, wasurenai yo 
After kissing good night</i>

00:23:33.550 --> 00:23:34.600
We're counting on you, man!

00:23:34.600 --> 00:23:35.930
Come through for us!

00:23:41.110 --> 00:23:47.320
<i>Yume yo, nemurenu yoru ni wa
Oh, dreams, take me away to that time</i>

00:23:43.980 --> 00:23:47.530
<i>We interrupt your regularly scheduled broadcast for the following urgent report.</i>

00:23:47.320 --> 00:23:53.910
<i>Tsuretette ano koro e
On those nights when I can't sleep</i>

00:23:48.820 --> 00:23:51.960
<i>Just moments ago, the Federation government announced</i>

00:23:51.960 --> 00:23:56.120
<i>that it will proceed with its initial plan to drop 
a photonic bomb on Graceland 24 hours from now.</i>

00:23:54.430 --> 00:23:59.870
<i>Nee...
 Okay?</i>

00:23:56.130 --> 00:23:57.800
<i>I repeat:</i>

00:23:57.800 --> 00:24:00.930
<i>Just moments ago, The Federation government announced</i>

00:24:00.930 --> 00:24:05.090
<i>that it will proceed with its initial plan to drop 
a photonic bomb on Graceland 24 hours from now.</i>

00:24:01.920 --> 00:24:05.420
Time left until the photonic bomb is dropped on Graceland...

00:24:05.420 --> 00:24:09.420
24 hours
